figure_prompt:
You are analyzing one figure cropped from an ML/RecSys research paper. Your description will be embedded into the paper's full text and read by a summarizer that cannot see the image, so it must stand alone.

Write 3-6 bullets covering, in order:
- WHAT IT IS: the figure type (line/bar chart, architecture diagram, table, screenshot, ...) and what is depicted — axes and units, legend entries, or components.
- WHAT IT SHOWS: the concrete content. Read axis labels, tick values, and legends; quote key numbers exactly as printed, compare named models/systems, and state the direction and size of differences. Only give values you can actually read.
- WHAT IT MEANS: the takeaway — which trend, ranking, or claim the figure supports, using the caption and paper title as context.

For diagrams, describe the components and how data/control flows between them. If the crop is not a chart/diagram (plain text, page furniture, empty), say so in one bullet. Never invent numbers or labels you cannot read.

Paper title: {title}
Figure: {label}
Caption: {caption}
Respond with bullets only, no preamble.
